# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS committed (this workspace produces binaries).

# --- Game data: NEVER commit ---
# The `GAME_DATA` folder: read-only runtime input, resolved through the `GAME_DATA` env var
# (docs/METHOD.md, "The data folder is read-only runtime input"). Its assets, and any code
# derived from it, live outside this repository by rule. `/GAME_DATA` is the dev link beside the
# checkout (a symlink to the real install, or an in-tree copy) — machine-local like the link,
# never committed; `scripts/data-guard.sh` fails the gates when anything under a resolved
# `GAME_DATA` is tracked.
/GAME_DATA
/GAME_DATA/

# Real data files used as test fixtures (document expected paths, do not commit).
**/tests/fixtures/

# --- the one folder the game persists into ---
# config, saves, settings. Machine-local by definition: `crates/spdesc`'s local-state module is
# the only thing in the tree that may write it.
/spdesc-config/

# Profiling output: `--features bevy/trace_chrome` drops a multi-GB flame chart in the cwd, which
# otherwise leaves the checkout "dirty".
trace-*.json

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
/.idea/
# Claude Code: settings and skills under .claude/ are each person's own.
/.claude/

# Python bytecode from the `scripts/` tooling.
__pycache__/

TASKBOARD.md
/*.log
